  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "round-heads-sahara-s014-p00150",
      "source_en": "Two different chronologies are thus proposed for the Bubaline style. According to the high one it is the most ancient phase of the Saharan rock art at, or before, 10,000 BP, the low one places it in the Neolithic period at around 7,500 BP. Regarding the final stages of the Bubaline style, the marker for the high chronology is the advent of pastoralism evidenced by the Pastoral style whereas the criteria for the low chronology is determined by the onset of arid conditions from 4,500 BP.",
